  "method": {
    "frozen": "Capture 206 dominant draws and their GPU resources in the original GLES context. Pause live rendering. Compare whole RGBA8 output using disposable readback copies, then five alternating rounds of original/two-way/no-portal controls, 40 samples after eight warmups per mode per round. GPU elapsed queries exclude setup, reset blits and readbacks; they include both candidate submissions.",
    "live": "Five matched original/two-way pairs with order reversed on alternating rounds, 1.5s settle and 4s measurement. Original shaders remain untouched. Intercept only the dominant root-domain mesh. One original-shader draw scissored to the checked rectangle, one separate shader outside it; outside shader contains XY rectangle rejection and no fragment-Z input or portal block. Per-logical-draw partitioning preserves interleaving with other particle draws.",
    "commonOverhead": "GL prototype uniform tracking, buffer mirroring and frame-plan projection remain in both modes. Candidate has extra uniform forwarding, program switches and a second draw; its measured CPU cost is real for this prototype but not a forecast for a differently integrated renderer. No V8 sampling, GPU readback, build or heavy analysis during timing windows.",
    "region": "Project root-sourced crossing triangles from mirrored float32 stream and UBO. Inflate by three pixels; nonpositive/near-zero clip-W uses a full-viewport fallback. This is a diagnostic guard, not a proved cross-device raster bound. GPU envelope reads verify bypassed pixels after each window and never select the region.",
    "scope": "Frozen numbers measure only dominant draws; live particle phase includes other particles. The user subsequently confirmed moving the character, explaining the changed view between earlier and newer captures. Exact before/after character and camera poses were not retained. New captures have different coverage, selected crossings, population and viewport from the earlier approximately 5ms view. Compare within these captures.",
    "boundary": "Nine triangle/depth shapes, three raster translations, finite/window/unbounded/uncovered modes, near-boundary offsets, depth enabled/disabled and single-mask/three-layer alpha-blend schedules. Envelope is unrestricted outside finite geometry. Compares complete RGBA8 outputs across two fresh processes; negative control replaces checked rectangle by an empty region.",
    "cleanup": {
      "restored": true
    }
  },
